bridge - an emulated switch
	ip link add bridge_name type bridge 
	ip link set bridge_name up  

netns - another 'logical' computers 
	ip netns add pc01 

veth - an emulated ethernet cable that connected between two kernel namespace 
	ip link add veth_left type veth peer name veth_right (this create one ethernet cable, each end has their own names) 
	ip link set veth_right netns pc01 (connect one side to the pc) 
	ip link set veth_left master bridge_name (connect the other side to switch)  
	
tap - an emulated ethernet cable that connected between kernel and user-space namespace (not used in this example)
	ip tuntap add dev tap0 mode tap
	ip link set tap0 up


after creating the devices and connect them (veth or tap), we need to turn them on 
ip link set veth_left up (turn on the swtich port)
ip -n pc01 ip link set lo up (turn on the computer loopback)
ip -n pc01 ip link set veth_left (turn on the computer ethernet)

add ip address to computer
ip -n pc01 addr add 192.168.0.11/24 dev veth_right

now we have successfully create a LAN 

below is to make the devices access internet 

turns the layer 2 swtich to layer 3 multilayer swtich that is able to do routing 
ip addr add 192.168.0.1/24 dev bridge_name 